  "correction_rules": [
    "Reduce forecast overshoots following sharp price spikes, especially when sentiment is neutral or negative.",
    "Adjust forecasts downward if recent history shows persistent mean reversion toward lower levels, particularly with negative sentiment.",
    "Apply a mild downward bias when sentiment is consistently positive but historical price action suggests overreaction.",
    "Increase downward correction magnitude if true outcomes lag behind forecasts by more than 2-3 days, especially in high-sentiment periods.",
    "Avoid overreacting to short-term sentiment shifts; maintain baseline correction for 3-5 days post-sentiment change unless confirmed reversal.",
    "Apply stronger downward adjustments when true outcomes are consistently below forecast, especially if sentiment is neutral or slightly positive."
  ]
